If the cluster exposes vector indexes, you create a vector index via the Mongo-style createIndex API with a vector index type option. Example (Mongo shell style, committing to a concrete form I would run):

db.products.createIndex(
  { product_embedding: 'vector' },
  {
    name: 'product_embedding_vec_idx',
    vectorIndexType: 'HNSW',
    vectorIndexOptions: { dims: 1536, similarity: 'cosine', m: 16, efConstruction: 200 }
  }
)

(Alternatives might use vectorIndexType: 'DiskANN' or 'IVF' and similar vectorIndexOptions.)
